      "text": "To find the product of $2.4$ and $0.2$, we can use the standard multiplication method. \n\nFirst, let's align the numbers by their decimal points:\n\n```\n  2.40\n× 0.2\n-----\n```\n\nNext, we multiply the numbers as if they were whole numbers:\n\n```\n  240\n×  20\n-----\n 4800\n```\n\nNow, we need to add the decimal point to the result. Since we have a total of 4 decimal places in the original numbers (2 from $2.4$ and 2 from $0.2$), we add a decimal point and 4 zeros to the right of the 4800:\n\n```\n  240\n×  20\n-----\n 4800.0\n```\n\nSo, $2.4 \\times 0.2 = 0.48$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{0.48}$.",
